      "text": "The framework adds process and context overhead, so direct agent execution is usually cheaper for well-scoped fixes, disposable experiments, or one-shot scripts with clear safe boundaries."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_940dff58a86bc5f6ae54f44aa4fe75d95ee06bd0a8ab380df4e5ee377f8452c5",
